---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { business } from "../data/business";

// Legal boilerplate. noindex and out of the sitemap, per project standard.
//
// This site belongs to the trading company itself, so - unlike some others in
// this portfolio - there is no separate site operator and no third-party
// contractor arrangement to explain. Contracts are made directly with
// LeonEast Roofing & Building Limited.
const hasEmail = Boolean(business.email);
const hasCompanyDetails = Boolean(business.companyNumber);
const updated = "10 September 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms & Conditions | LeonEast Roofing & Building"
  description="The terms on which LeonEast Roofing & Building provides surveys, quotations and roofing work, and how the workmanship guarantee applies."
  noindex={true}
>
  <section class="bg-ink text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight">
        <a href="/" class="text-white hover:text-brand-light transition-colors">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-steel-light">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 prose prose-stone max-w-none">
    <h2>About us and this website</h2>
    <p>
      This website is owned and operated by {business.name}
      {hasCompanyDetails
        ? `, a company registered in England and Wales under number ${business.companyNumber}`
        : ", a limited company registered in England and Wales"}.
      Any contract for surveys, quotations or roofing work arising from this website is made
      directly with us.
    </p>

    <h2>Information on this site</h2>
    <p>
      The guidance, price bands and local information published here are provided in good
      faith and in general terms. They are not a substitute for a survey of your particular
      roof, and nothing on this website constitutes a quotation or an offer to carry out work
      at a stated price. Price ranges are indicative and intended to help you budget and
      compare quotations sensibly.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where we refer to planning rules, conservation areas, Article 4 directions or building
      regulations, we do so to help you know what to check. Those rules change and their
      application depends on your specific property, so please confirm the position with the
      relevant local authority before relying on it.
    </p>

    <h2>Surveys and quotations</h2>
    <p>
      Surveys are carried out free of charge and place you under no obligation. A quotation
      issued following a survey is fixed for the work described in it and remains open for
      thirty days unless it states otherwise. It covers only what is itemised. Where a defect
      is genuinely concealed and cannot be identified until the covering is opened up - for
      example rot in rafter feet or a wall plate, or an unsound chimney - the quotation will
      say so, and any additional work will be described, priced and agreed with you in writing
      before it is carried out.
    </p>

    <h2>Carrying out the work</h2>
    <p>
      We will agree a start date with you and keep you informed if weather prevents work from
      proceeding, which on roofing it sometimes will. We will not leave a roof open overnight.
      Access equipment remains our responsibility and must not be used or altered by anyone
      else. Please keep the working area clear and, where relevant, keep children and pets
      away from it while we are on site.
    </p>

    <h2>Payment</h2>
    <p>
      Repairs are invoiced on completion and payable within the period stated on the invoice.
      On larger works such as a full re-roof, where materials and access are purchased in
      advance, staged payments may apply; the stages and amounts will be set out on the
      quotation before you accept it. Title in materials passes to you on payment. We do not
      ask for large cash deposits.
    </p>

    <h2>The workmanship guarantee</h2>
    <p>
      Work we complete carries a {business.workmanshipGuaranteeYears} year guarantee on our
      workmanship, issued to you in writing at completion. If a defect arises in that
      workmanship within the guarantee period we will return and put it right at no cost to
      you.
    </p>
    <p>
      The guarantee covers our work. It does not cover a new and unrelated defect elsewhere on
      the roof, damage caused by a subsequent storm or other event, damage caused by third
      parties working on the roof after us, or failure arising from lack of ordinary
      maintenance such as blocked gutters. Materials carry their manufacturers' own warranties
      on their own terms, and the applicable warranty will be identified in your completion
      paperwork.
    </p>

    <h2>Your cancellation rights</h2>
    <p>
      Where a contract is agreed away from our business premises - which for a domestic
      roofing job it usually is - you have a statutory right to cancel within fourteen days
      under the Consumer Contracts (Information, Cancellation and Additional Charges)
      Regulations 2013. If you have asked us in writing to begin work within that period and
      then cancel, we may charge for the work already carried out. Your cancellation rights
      will be set out with your quotation.
    </p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>
      We maintain public liability insurance. Nothing in these terms excludes or limits our
      liability for death or personal injury caused by our negligence, for fraud, or for
      anything else which cannot lawfully be excluded. Your statutory rights as a consumer,
      including the right to work carried out with reasonable care and skill under the
      Consumer Rights Act 2015, are not affected by anything on this page.
    </p>

    <h2>Complaints</h2>
    <p>
      If something is not right, please tell us as soon as possible on
      {" "}<a href={business.phoneHref}>{business.phone}</a>
      {hasEmail && <> or by email at <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a></>}.
      We would far rather come back and sort it out than have you unhappy with a roof we
      worked on.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms and any contract arising from them are governed by the law of England and
      Wales, and are subject to the jurisdiction of the courts of England and Wales.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
